  "conclusion": "corresponds",
  "rationale": "base_step_correspondence is an iff for arbitrary class tables and Given configurations, with arbitrary Shared after on the LHS and an existential Given successor plus exact embedding equality on the RHS. It covers GC and exit without WF premises, so it is both forward preservation and reflection of all successors, exactly as stated. The machine/gc/steps units introduce the lifetime notation; inherited syntax, storage and typing notation remain in the listed dependency units. Functions keeps its explicit inherited-machinery forward reference to the appendix.",
